      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Perpetually storing even just enough of your ID to reliably determine that it's been used before is ludicrous, and I have no doubt that they will store more than that. I once had my SSN leaked by a third party address service to my healthcare provider that had no business even receiving my SSN from them, because companies with data are appealing targets. People seem to have no idea how dangerous this kind of data is and it should be the #1 concern they have.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
