      "statusChangeID": "676216da9a5f88aedfb6ca44",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "In line with this request:\n\n> the system should only be looking at confirming A. the ID is the user’s and B. the birthdate is over 18 years ago.\n\nOur recent changes illustrated [in this video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lzG9IwmM7TI) demonstrate how the system works. \n\nWe validate that the ID belongs to the user, create a non-reversible hash to ensure the validity of the ID, and then save the user's birth date and the hash. All other data is deleted. [Please see our FAQ thread for more details.](https://ask.vrchat.com/t/age-verification-faq/28458#p-58953-new-the-changes-video-mentioned-a-hash-what-is-that-13)\n\nKeeping your birth date is necessitated by our regulatory requirement to adhere to COPPA, as well as allowing us to update Verification state when users reach their 18th birthday. VRChat has always collected the user birth date upon their first-time agreement with our Terms of Service.\n\nSince these updates address the core feedback of this post, I'm marking it as completed.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
